1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,066
For seven lectures, nobody has left the ship.

2
00:00:03,966 --> 00:00:06,399
Today, at last, somebody does.

3
00:00:08,199 --> 00:00:09,821
The ship stops at the door,

4
00:00:10,271 --> 00:00:12,890
and one of the crew goes in wearing a suit.

5
00:00:13,790 --> 00:00:16,386
They read the altar,

6
00:00:16,836 --> 00:00:18,794
they cut through a fallen slab,

7
00:00:19,244 --> 00:00:20,984
and they bring out the bowl by hand.

8
00:00:22,784 --> 00:00:25,663
And the part that surprised me is how little there is to write.

9
00:00:26,863 --> 00:00:29,088
Going outside is called EVA,

10
00:00:29,538 --> 00:00:31,674
and most of it is already in your mission.

11
00:00:32,574 --> 00:00:36,760
The game offers the crew a way out, at the door of any ruin you build.

12
00:00:37,660 --> 00:00:39,380
It puts them in a suit,

13
00:00:39,830 --> 00:00:42,192
it gives the suit a list of your places,

14
00:00:42,642 --> 00:00:45,235
and it flies the suit to the one they pick.

15
00:00:47,035 --> 00:00:49,203
You wrote the door in Lecture three.

16
00:00:49,653 --> 00:00:51,470
It's the place with the role entrance.

17
00:00:52,370 --> 00:00:55,780
The offer is made while the ship is within three thousand of that place,

18
00:00:56,230 --> 00:00:58,392
and it's taken back when the ship leaves.

19
00:00:59,292 --> 00:01:01,494
But not while somebody is still outside.

20
00:01:02,694 --> 00:01:05,165
A crew member in a suit gets a console of their own,

21
00:01:05,615 --> 00:01:07,936
with a handheld that has five apps.

22
00:01:08,836 --> 00:01:10,448
Nav is the list of places.

23
00:01:10,898 --> 00:01:12,642
Act is what a place says.

24
00:01:13,092 --> 00:01:14,645
Scan reads the room.

25
00:01:15,095 --> 00:01:16,739
Fire holds the tools.

26
00:01:17,189 --> 00:01:19,512
And Crew is the way home.

27
00:01:21,312 --> 00:01:22,840
There are three things to remember.

28
00:01:23,740 --> 00:01:26,607
A suit flies to places, and to nothing else.

29
00:01:27,057 --> 00:01:28,735
You can't steer it by hand.

30
00:01:29,635 --> 00:01:33,084
A hidden place isn't on the list until it's been found.

31
00:01:33,984 --> 00:01:36,967
And the tools reach six hundred, and no further.

32
00:01:38,167 --> 00:01:39,496
Now the first new record.

33
00:01:40,396 --> 00:01:43,368
A barrier is a ball of blocked space.

34
00:01:43,818 --> 00:01:47,134
Every way through it is shut, until somebody opens it.

35
00:01:48,934 --> 00:01:50,709
But look at what I type first.

36
00:01:51,159 --> 00:01:53,370
It's a place, on the near side of the door.

37
00:01:54,270 --> 00:01:56,776
That's because a suit can only fly to places,

38
00:01:57,226 --> 00:01:59,392
and its cutter only reaches six hundred.

39
00:02:00,292 --> 00:02:02,124
With no place beside the slab,

40
00:02:02,574 --> 00:02:05,117
nobody could ever get close enough to cut it.

41
00:02:06,917 --> 00:02:08,881
Then the slab itself.

42
00:02:09,781 --> 00:02:13,387
Barrier, three numbers for where, and one for how big.

43
00:02:14,287 --> 00:02:16,440
And Clear with, beam,

44
00:02:16,890 --> 00:02:18,743
which means the suit's cutter opens it.

45
00:02:19,943 --> 00:02:22,712
When a barrier opens, the game sends a word.

46
00:02:23,612 --> 00:02:26,653
It's the barrier's key, and then underscore opened.

47
00:02:27,103 --> 00:02:28,776
Mine is slab opened.

48
00:02:30,576 --> 00:02:32,642
So I write a step that waits for it.

49
00:02:33,542 --> 00:02:35,014
It goes after the altar,

50
00:02:35,464 --> 00:02:37,659
and the altar's step now reveals this one.

51
00:02:38,559 --> 00:02:40,078
I don't send that word anywhere.

52
00:02:40,528 --> 00:02:41,416
The game sends it,

53
00:02:41,866 --> 00:02:44,499
however the slab comes open.

54
00:02:46,299 --> 00:02:48,509
Under the first sentence there's a short list,

55
00:02:48,959 --> 00:02:50,678
and each bullet is a little picture.

56
00:02:51,578 --> 00:02:54,878
A hyphen and a space, then the picture, then the words.

57
00:02:55,778 --> 00:02:57,214
A person for suiting up,

58
00:02:57,664 --> 00:02:59,713
and a flame for the cut.

59
00:03:00,613 --> 00:03:02,621
Lint doesn't check the picture's name,

60
00:03:03,071 --> 00:03:04,550
so copy it from the page.

61
00:03:05,750 --> 00:03:09,365
Last time Comms said the final word, in a call.

62
00:03:10,265 --> 00:03:14,049
Since Lecture five the game says it, when the bowl is taken.

63
00:03:14,499 --> 00:03:16,964
So Comms stops saying it.

64
00:03:18,764 --> 00:03:21,204
But there's a trap here, and it's worth a minute.

65
00:03:22,104 --> 00:03:24,538
The walls of a ruin don't hold a ship.

66
00:03:25,438 --> 00:03:28,700
So a ship could fly in and scoop up the bowl early,

67
00:03:29,150 --> 00:03:31,255
before the last step was listening.

68
00:03:32,155 --> 00:03:33,572
The word would be spent,

69
00:03:34,022 --> 00:03:36,146
and the story could never end.

70
00:03:37,946 --> 00:03:41,071
So I don't let the bowl exist yet.

71
00:03:41,971 --> 00:03:44,747
Comms gets a new answer, open the niche,

72
00:03:45,197 --> 00:03:47,004
and it sends a word of my own.

73
00:03:47,904 --> 00:03:52,618
And the niche says starts when, signal, that word.

74
00:03:54,418 --> 00:03:57,069
The step is always listening before the bowl is there.

75
00:03:57,969 --> 00:03:59,758
Then I change the objective,

76
00:04:00,208 --> 00:04:02,379
and I delete the quest from Lecture five,

77
00:04:02,829 --> 00:04:04,618
because the arc does its job now.

78
00:04:05,818 --> 00:04:09,252
I don't want the game to end with somebody still outside.

79
00:04:10,152 --> 00:04:12,793
So taking the bowl reveals one more step,

80
00:04:13,243 --> 00:04:15,538
and that one is finished back at the station.

81
00:04:16,438 --> 00:04:20,101
Its second paragraph tells the crew to count heads first.

82
00:04:21,901 --> 00:04:23,347
And I give the crew more time.

83
00:04:24,247 --> 00:04:26,043
A suit is slower than a ship.

84
00:04:26,493 --> 00:04:31,082
In my test it took about three minutes from the door to the altar.

85
00:04:31,982 --> 00:04:34,916
So twenty minutes becomes forty,

86
00:04:35,366 --> 00:04:37,674
in the fence and in the last paragraph.

87
00:04:38,874 --> 00:04:40,816
I run lint, and it's clean.

88
00:04:41,716 --> 00:04:43,878
Now I misspell the word on the step,

89
00:04:44,328 --> 00:04:46,147
and lint says nothing sends it.

90
00:04:47,047 --> 00:04:48,258
That's what I want.

91
00:04:50,058 --> 00:04:52,748
Next I delete the place beside the slab,

92
00:04:53,198 --> 00:04:54,990
and lint says clean.

93
00:04:55,890 --> 00:04:58,524
But that mission can't be finished.

94
00:04:59,424 --> 00:05:01,324
The slab is out of everyone's reach,

95
00:05:01,774 --> 00:05:05,257
and no file can tell lint how far a cutter reaches.

96
00:05:07,057 --> 00:05:09,654
So that's the check to do by eye.

97
00:05:10,104 --> 00:05:13,059
Every barrier needs a place within six hundred of it.

98
00:05:14,259 --> 00:05:16,620
I fly to the door, and I stop the ship.

99
00:05:17,520 --> 00:05:20,764
On my handheld there's a Boarding Party app,

100
00:05:21,214 --> 00:05:23,381
and its button says suit up.

101
00:05:25,181 --> 00:05:26,409
And now I'm outside.

102
00:05:27,309 --> 00:05:30,618
I pick the Altar from the list, and the suit flies itself.

103
00:05:32,418 --> 00:05:35,622
And here are the words I wrote four lectures ago,

104
00:05:36,072 --> 00:05:38,500
read by somebody standing in front of the table.

105
00:05:39,400 --> 00:05:41,674
On Comms I mark the Gallery,

106
00:05:42,124 --> 00:05:43,894
and the Niche joins my list.

107
00:05:44,794 --> 00:05:47,606
I pick it, and Nav says there's no way through.

108
00:05:49,406 --> 00:05:51,483
So I go to the Gallery Door.

109
00:05:52,383 --> 00:05:54,182
On Fire there's the slab.

110
00:05:54,632 --> 00:05:58,337
I select it, I press again, and I wait twelve seconds.

111
00:05:59,237 --> 00:06:00,340
The step is done.

112
00:06:02,140 --> 00:06:03,699
Now for the niche.

113
00:06:04,599 --> 00:06:06,664
Comms opens it, and there's the bowl.

114
00:06:07,114 --> 00:06:09,922
I take it, I come aboard, and we fly home.

115
00:06:10,822 --> 00:06:11,863
And that's the game.

116
00:06:13,063 --> 00:06:14,066
Now it's your turn.

117
00:06:14,966 --> 00:06:18,185
Let an engineer work the slab loose by hand.

118
00:06:19,085 --> 00:06:21,678
Make the slab open by itself.

119
00:06:22,578 --> 00:06:24,304
Send someone out for the canisters.

120
00:06:26,104 --> 00:06:28,523
Then break one line where lint can see it,

121
00:06:28,973 --> 00:06:30,348
and one where it can't.

122
00:06:31,248 --> 00:06:34,608
Next time, the same suit goes to work outside a station.
